---
# Model of the figure 'bus-timing'. Edit this file; `kokeb-docs figures` draws it. Never edit the SVGs.
# Every number is a param with the datasheet section and page it comes from (`ref`, a name under refs here or in
# docs/hardware.yml); a number without one fails the build. Wave characters and keys: docs/figkit.md in ci-tools.
kind: timing
id: bus-timing
title: UART character
kicker: On the bus
alt: >-
  One UART character of the XMPL100 on its TX line: the start bit, eight data bits least significant first and the
  stop bit, at the bit rate of the datasheet.
reads: >-
  The lane is TX, left to right in time. The line idles high, the start bit pulls it low for one bit time, the data
  bits D0 to D7 follow and the stop bit returns it high. The table under the lane gives the bit rate.
print: landscape
sources:
  - docs/model/bus-timing.timing.yml
bus: uart
refs:
  uart: {doc: ds, section: "6.2 UART interface", page: 8}
signals:
  - {id: tx, label: TX, wave: "10========1", data: [D0, D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7]}
groups:
  - {from: 1, to: 2, label: start}
  - {from: 2, to: 10, label: "8 data bits, LSB first", ref: uart}
  - {from: 10, to: 11, label: stop}
params:
  - {id: baud, symbol: baud, label: Bit rate, typ: 115200, unit: bit/s, ref: uart}
